# =============================================================================
# Docker / BuildKit Build Context Ignore Rules
# =============================================================================
# Matches `.gcloudignore` (using `**/` recursive globs for Docker's pattern
# matcher) so local `docker build` and Cloud Build Docker steps never send
# virtual environments, caches, Terraform state/secrets, or generated archives
# into the build context.
#
# Preserves all runtime and workshop assets required for builds & manifests:
#   Dockerfile, main.py, requirements.txt, pyproject.toml,
#   agents-cli-manifest.yaml, services.py, services.yaml,
#   coding_agent/, skills_to_register/
# =============================================================================

# Ignore metadata and VCS files
.dockerignore
.gcloudignore
.git
.gitignore

# Python virtual environments, bytecode, and build/test caches
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
**/*.egg-info/

# Local environment secrets (never include .env files in build context)
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Terraform directory, caches, state, variables, and generated archives
terraform/
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate*
**/*.tfvars*
**/*.tar.gz

# Generated evaluation traces, reports, and optimization outputs
**/artifacts/

# OS / editor noise
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
